    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0248" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg128"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic">January 6,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 51.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of to-day’s date, in which you kindly inform me that you have
                    received absolutely certain information that the American proprietors of the
                    Canton and Hankau Railway, to meet the criticisms and objections <pb facs="0249"
                        n="129" xml:id="pg129"/> which have been made in China to the concession,
                    have regained control of the complete ownership of a clear bona fide majority of
                    the entire stock of that company.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to state that I have cabled your entire note to my
                    government for its consideration.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chentung
                    Liang-Cheng.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
